From: MasherDon <62326358+MasherDon@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sun, 25 Oct 2026 20:35:39 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 097/121] graph + mmap + model : SiegeLadder P8d - the Engram
 tables unmapped, every row read straight from the model files (on by default,
 LLAMA_ENGRAM_UNMAPPED=0 - off). At load the files that hold nothing
 host-resident but engram tables (on 1017: the two 98 GB FP8 tables and layer
 1's 3 GB scale table, 186 GiB) are released like the expert files; a table
 that is a copied host tensor (layer 14's scales, in a streamed expert file)
 stays in RAM and is read from there (llama_model::engram_w_disk /
 engram_s_disk). At decode G26's helper (read_ahead) reads the ubatch's rows
 into dec_rows - fill_layer takes them when its own hashes match, else reads
 them itself; in prompts P8's helper always reads directly (P8c's path, now
 through llm_graph_input_engram::read_rows). llama_read_scattered keeps one
 unbuffered overlapped handle per file for the process, asks BypassIO for it
 (FSCTL_MANAGE_BYPASS_IO) and reads on the caller's thread when n_thr is 1.
 Why: Windows checks every unbuffered read of a mapped file for cache
 coherency - diskspd on a mapped engram file 13K 4 KB reads a second, unmapped
 0.72M, with BypassIO 1.14M; cached reads of the mapped file 0.2-0.44M, no
 better than PrefetchVirtualMemory (SiegeLadder runs.md 4.240). Bitwise the
 same logits as the mapped path at -ub 4096 and -ub 32
 (bench/engram_pp_check.py arms u / m). A B B A: agent turns 2-8 read in 48.0
 / 47.7 s against 50.6 / 50.1 (-5%; turn 7.5K +10%), answers 18.37 / 18.30
 tok/s against 17.89 / 17.60 (+3%), cold 2.2K / 8.9K +2% / +6%, the turns'
 paging 350-860 MB -> 9-120 MB

