+    // SiegeLadder P8d (on by default, LLAMA_ENGRAM_UNMAPPED=0 - off): the engram tables leave the mapping - the files
+    // that hold nothing host-resident but engram tables (on 1017: the two 98 GB FP8 tables and layer 1's 3 GB scale
+    // table) are released here, as the loader releases the expert files, and their rows are read with unbuffered
+    // overlapped I/O (llama_read_scattered). While a file is mapped, Windows checks every unbuffered read of it for cache
+    // coherency: 13K reads a second on a mapped engram file against 0.7-1.1M unmapped (SiegeLadder runs.md 4.238, 4.240),
+    // so the direct reads of P8c pay only here. A table that is a copied host tensor (copy_host_from) stays in RAM.
+    // Bitwise the same logits; agent turns 2-8 read 5% faster (turn 7.5K +10%), cold 2.2K / 8.9K +2% / +6%, answers +3%,
